# Separate Editor save correction

This stage derives from immutable accepted search/path126 and is authored only after the UI-negative166 and queued-revision-negative26 epochs were frozen. Both negative inventories, exact failed source/logs and observations remain unchanged. No production or shared-host files were edited.

A Save response updates the committed saved baseline, revision and byte count, while preserving the document's current content. Typing remains enabled; a per-document pending flag refuses duplicate requests. Late successful/failed responses publish only to a mounted view that still owns the same document object, and status publication is limited to that active document. Closed/reopened or disposed views cannot accept the old item response. Another open document can save independently. The server captures the primitive revision before any await/queue, matching its existing path/content capture; this fixes a direct shared-object precondition issue, not an HTTP JSON exploit.

Focused verification passed 41/41 with zero failures/skips/cancellations and 28 source fingerprints stable before/after. Seven exact UI-negative/control bodies and three exact queued-revision bodies were replayed with only import paths changed; they pass 7/7 and 3/3. Thirty-one selected app/save/read/search/path/UI/HTTP regressions include four new actual-client controls. The unchanged Git CLI and sequence-diff suites were not rerun. No original engine or benchmark/profiling run occurred. These are finite actual-module element models and in-process HTTP hosts, not actual browser or original full workbench verification.

The previously reproduced typing loss now retains the newer dirty draft through navigation and comparison while disk still contains only the captured write. The queued stale mutation now rejects while the first accepted commit remains intact. Actual conflict/reopen retry, duplicate keyboard refusal with typing enabled, disposed activation and B save while A response is held passed. Exact raw logs and source snapshots are retained.

Only client.mjs, server.mjs and app README differ from accepted126; save-publication.ui.test.mjs is added. Source-only copies of shared staging host/library/catalog files are exact baseline dependencies for tests and are not proposed installation changes. New independent acceptance is pending. No whole-editor parity, universal behavior, all-feature or superiority claim is made. An already committed disk write cannot be cancelled by closing a tab; existing live filesystem race and unsaved-recovery limitations remain.

The focused receipt's output-limit field was named combined; the actual unchanged spawnSync option applies 4 MiB independently to stdout and stderr. The final receipt states the actual limit, and validation-metadata-clarification.json preserves this correction without changing the original source, raw outputs or focused receipt. Three test controller children also launched Node's per-file test workers; completed finite runs do not establish universal Windows descendant cleanup.
